// endpoint_revise_response.proto — ReviseResponse: rewrite one settled response
// whole, out of the conversation's sight. AGENT section.
//
// THE USER ASKED ABOUT WORDS THEY HIGHLIGHTED in a final response, and the
// answer is a revised version of that response rather than a new turn. The
// daemon composes the whole instruction (the response, the highlighted words
// and what the user said, images included); the shim runs it on a SIDE QUERY
// and writes the answer as the page line
// conversation.v1.AgentUpdate.response_revision.
//
// THE SIDE QUERY IS A THROWAWAY FORK THAT PERSISTS NOTHING. It resumes the
// session's own conversation through the newest finished turn (the same point
// GetForkPoint names), so it reads the response in the context it was written
// in, from the prompt cache, and a turn in flight is never part of it. It forks
// to a vendor session that is never written, so the session's transcript is
// untouched and the live query, its turn and its locks are never involved: a
// revision runs beside a turn in flight.
//
// UNARY, AND IT RETURNS ONCE THE REVISION IS WRITTEN. `success` means the page
// line was handed to the store; the revised prose reaches the daemon on the
// main agent's stream like every other page line. The call's lifetime is the
// revision's: a caller that goes away cancels it, and nothing is written.

